# Deliberately empty of values.
#
# `wrangler types` reads `.dev.vars` when it is not told otherwise, so the
# generated `worker-configuration.d.ts` picked up whichever secrets happened to
# be on the machine that ran it — and `wrangler types --check` then failed for
# everybody else, including CI and a fresh clone, with a stale-types error that
# was not real. Pointing `--env-file` here replaces that discovery, so the file
# is generated from `wrangler.jsonc` alone and is byte-identical everywhere.
#
# Secrets are typed by hand in `src/secrets.d.ts`, which is the honest place for
# them: a secret is set with `wrangler secret put`, never in Worker config, so
# no generator can know about it. Add new ones there, not here.
